<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="FB_DeviceDiagnostics" Id="{1c5e8a37-6d92-4b04-8f17-3a9e0c2b5d64}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    Derives LinkStatus/DataStatus/ConnectionStatus for a common EtherCAT slave from its
    State/WcState/InputToggle PDO inputs.

    Purpose:
        Turn the three standard PDO signals an EtherCAT slave exposes - the ESM state word,
        the working-counter state and the input toggle heartbeat - into one link verdict, one
        data-freshness verdict and one combined connection verdict, so that callers and EPICS
        consumers no longer decode the raw bits themselves.

    Usage:
        Declare one instance per slave, read the block's documentation and I_DeviceDiagnostics
        for the contract, and call it every PLC cycle - it is non-blocking and holds only
        TON/R_TRIG state. Link the raw inputs to the slave's PDO tree in the IO mapping (State
        under InfoData, WcState/InputToggle under WcState); they are %I* terminals, so assign
        them through the IO mapping rather than from ST:

            fbDiag : FB_DeviceDiagnostics;

            fbDiag(tStaleTimeout := T#5S);
            IF fbDiag.ConnectionStatus <> E_DeviceConnectionStatus.Connected THEN
                // slave not operational, working counter failing, or inputs stale
            END_IF

        tStaleTimeout is the only tunable: the longest InputToggle may stay unchanged before
        DataStatus reports Stale. LinkStatus reports the raw ESM state, DataStatus reports
        WcError/Stale/Ok, and ConnectionStatus gates the latter on the former, so a consumer
        can tell "off the bus" from "up but inputs stopped updating".

    Objectives:
        - Keep the three verdicts separate so a fault can be classified without inspecting
          raw PDO values.
        - Never block the PLC cycle: stale detection is a TON restarted on every toggle edge.
        - Stay device-model agnostic - only the three standard PDO signals are consumed.
        - Expose the verdicts as pytmc-tagged PVs through I_DeviceDiagnostics.

    History:
        2026-08-20 Mandza        - Original version (I_DeviceDiagnostics and this block).
        2026-08-23 Mandza        - Stop gating DataStatus on LinkStatus; support both
                                   WcState shapes.
        2026-11-27 Audit finding - Completed the header (purpose/usage/objectives/history)
                                   and added a header to every property Get accessor.
*)
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_DeviceDiagnostics IMPLEMENTS I_DeviceDiagnostics
VAR_INPUT
    tStaleTimeout : TIME := T#5S; // max time InputToggle may stay unchanged before DataStatus reports Stale
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    {attribute 'pytmc' := 'pv: LinkStatus
        io: i
        field: DESC EtherCAT slave state machine state'}
    eLinkStatus       : E_EcCommState;
    {attribute 'pytmc' := 'pv: DataStatus
        io: i
        field: DESC WcState/InputToggle combined'}
    eDataStatus       : E_DataStatus;
    {attribute 'pytmc' := 'pv: ConnectionStatus
        io: i
        field: DESC Combined device diagnostic verdict'}
    eConnectionStatus : E_DeviceConnectionStatus;
END_VAR
VAR
    nState AT %I* : WORD;
    {attribute 'pytmc' := 'pv: WcState
        io: i
        field: DESC Working counter state
        field: ZNAM OK
        field: ONAM Error'}
    bWcState AT %I* : BOOL;
    {attribute 'pytmc' := 'pv: InputToggle
        io: i'}
    bInputToggle AT %I* : BOOL;

    rToggleRise : R_TRIG;
    fToggleFall : F_TRIG;
    tonStale    : TON;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[eLinkStatus := nState AND 16#000F;

// restart the stale timer on every toggle edge
rToggleRise(CLK := bInputToggle);
fToggleFall(CLK := bInputToggle);
tonStale(IN := NOT (rToggleRise.Q OR fToggleFall.Q), PT := tStaleTimeout);

IF bWcState THEN
    eDataStatus := E_DataStatus.WcError;
ELSIF tonStale.Q THEN
    eDataStatus := E_DataStatus.Stale;
ELSE
    eDataStatus := E_DataStatus.Ok;
END_IF

IF eLinkStatus <> E_EcCommState.eEcState_OP THEN
    eConnectionStatus := E_DeviceConnectionStatus.NotOperational;
ELSE
    CASE eDataStatus OF
        E_DataStatus.WcError: eConnectionStatus := E_DeviceConnectionStatus.WcError;
        E_DataStatus.Stale:   eConnectionStatus := E_DeviceConnectionStatus.Stale;
    ELSE
        eConnectionStatus := E_DeviceConnectionStatus.Connected;
    END_CASE
END_IF
]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Property Name="LinkStatus" Id="{2d6f9b48-7e03-4c15-9028-4b0d1e3c6f75}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[PROPERTY LinkStatus : E_EcCommState]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{3e70ac59-8f14-4d26-a139-5c1e2f4d7086}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    Get accessor for LinkStatus.

    Purpose:
        Hand the decoded EtherCAT state machine state of the slave to the caller, so that
        the link verdict can be read without touching the raw State PDO word (nState).

    Usage:
        Read-only and side-effect free; may be evaluated every cycle, e.g.
        IF fbDiag.LinkStatus <> E_EcCommState.eEcState_OP THEN. Implements the abstract
        property declared in I_DeviceDiagnostics.

    Objectives:
        - Return exactly the low nibble of the State PDO (the ESM state value, where
          eEcState_OP = 8) and nothing else.
        - Keep the bit masking in this block so consumers see a typed enum instead of a
          raw WORD.

    History:
        2026-08-21 Mandza        - Original version.
        2026-11-27 Audit finding - Added this accessor header.
*)
VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
                <Implementation>
                    <ST><![CDATA[LinkStatus := eLinkStatus;]]></ST>
                </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="DataStatus" Id="{4f81bd6a-9025-4e37-b24a-6d2f304e8197}">
            <Declaration><![CDATA[PROPERTY DataStatus : E_DataStatus]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{5092ce7b-a136-4f48-c35b-7e304152f2a8}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    Get accessor for DataStatus.

    Purpose:
        Report whether the slave's inbound process data is usable - working counter error,
        stale heartbeat, or OK - as computed by the cyclic logic of this block.

    Usage:
        Read-only and side-effect free; may be evaluated every cycle, e.g.
        IF fbDiag.DataStatus <> E_DataStatus.Ok THEN. It reflects the previous call to the
        block body, so call the block before reading this property. Implements the abstract
        property declared in I_DeviceDiagnostics.

    Objectives:
        - Let a consumer distinguish a working-counter error (a frame went missing) from a
          stale heartbeat (the slave stopped toggling its inputs).
        - Return a typed E_DataStatus rather than the raw bWcState/tonStale.Q pair.

    History:
        2026-08-21 Mandza        - Original version.
        2026-11-27 Audit finding - Added this accessor header.
*)
VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
                <Implementation>
                    <ST><![CDATA[DataStatus := eDataStatus;]]></ST>
                </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
    <Property Name="ConnectionStatus" Id="{61a3df8c-b247-4059-d46c-8f4152630309}">
      <Declaration><![CDATA[PROPERTY ConnectionStatus : E_DeviceConnectionStatus]]></Declaration>
      <Get Name="Get" Id="{72b4e09d-c358-4160-e57d-90526374141a}">
        <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    Get accessor for ConnectionStatus.

    Purpose:
        Report the single combined diagnostic verdict for the slave - NotOperational,
        WcError, Stale or Connected - which is what most callers and the EPICS PV actually
        want to branch on.

    Usage:
        Read-only and side-effect free; may be evaluated every cycle, e.g.
        IF fbDiag.ConnectionStatus <> E_DeviceConnectionStatus.Connected THEN. Refreshed by
        the block body, so call the block before reading it. Implements the abstract property
        declared in I_DeviceDiagnostics.

    Objectives:
        - Collapse LinkStatus and DataStatus into one verdict without hiding the underlying
          reason, so downstream alarms can still log the detail from the two enums.
        - Report NotOperational whenever the ESM state is not OP, and otherwise pass the
          DataStatus verdict through.

    History:
        2026-08-21 Mandza        - Original version.
        2026-11-27 Audit finding - Added this accessor header.
*)
VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
                <Implementation>
                    <ST><![CDATA[ConnectionStatus := eConnectionStatus;]]></ST>
                </Implementation>
      </Get>
    </Property>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>
